WEBVTT

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.740
See you, Yuri.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.960
See you, Commander Yulanov.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:55.290
I think it's time the chameleon had a little facelift.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.140
With the face of the Soviet space chief, the top secret laser guidance codes will be ours for the taking!

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.590
Now he did

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:50.300
Cheat job chasing

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.380
As you know, Warfield has established an exchange program with its sister academy in Moscow.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.900
The four of you have been chosen to go to Moscow for a week.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.870
Too bad we aren't improving relations with the Hawaiians.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.210
I hear the surfing's lousy in Moscow.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.370
Mr. Milbanks, the Russian students have just arrived,

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.950
and the van is ready to take our group to the airport.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.980
Well, take good care of them, Mr. Mitchell.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.540
Oh, and make sure they set a shining example for the Russians.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:29.670
Yes, sir.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.060
Do svidani, Mr. Milbanks.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.360
Well, goodbye, James.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.150
James, you forgot something.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.360
It's my latest invention, an umbrella satellite dish.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:49.620
It'll not only keep you dry, but you can communicate with anyone in the world, including me.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.400
One more thing, James.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:53.840
IQ.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:59.500
I know, I know, you already packed gloves, but these are special.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.640
I put vibrational amplifiers in the fingertips.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.380
They'll give you super sensitive touch.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.910
Say, you're right, IQ.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.090
These are sensitive.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.790
I think I feel something.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:12.820
Very funny.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.460
I'll pay you back as soon as I return from Moscow.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:27.570
You're clear of a jerk named Trevor Noseworthy the fourth.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.860
Hello, Trevor Noseworthy IV. Welcome to Warfield.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:41.340
Well, I suppose Siberia isn't the only thing cold in Russia.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:48.420
Space station crew have been in orbit for six months.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.210
They will be very happy to be home.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.080
I'm sure they will, General.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.250
Ah, here they come now.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.860
to see you, sir. Have you got the red star

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.100
born laser coats?

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.160
You'll excuse me, gentlemen, but I have

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.240
to get this back to the launch pad and turn it over

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.780
to our new space station crew.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.150
Commander Yulanov is getting into his car.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:38.450
The Minister of Internal Affairs thinks the Space Chief may try to sell the laser phones.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:39.410
Follow him.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:39.930
Yeah.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:51.170
Like I said, it was ours for the taking.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.660
Good work, Chameleon.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:59.200
Oh, by the way, I never got a chance to introduce our newest henchmen.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.840
Or should I say, hench-women!

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.040
I'm Max! This is my partner, Joe!

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.320
Well, we might as well make this a face-to-face introduction.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:15.790
It's not Commander Yulanov! Come on!

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.540
Go to range, we've got to get to the launch site!

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.040
Not before we make a little switch.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:27.540
Once the new cosmonaut crew programs our codes into the space station superlaser,

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.900
we'll be able to aim the laser from the ground.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.700
and slice open the 10-foot steel walls of the Russian Treasury Reserve.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.560
Yes, and help ourselves to the entire Russian Reserve of Diamonds and Rubies.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.800
Your plan has just come to an end, derange.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:48.530
Plan A, perhaps, but plan B is about to begin.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.240
Max, Joe.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:12.620
Save them! They'll be sleeping soundly for days, as will the real Commander Ulyanov.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:16.730
Let's move it! Wouldn't want to be late for the launch, would we?

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.670
No, we wouldn't, would we, Dr. DeRay?

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:28.570
Welcome to Moscow Academy. Let me introduce your classmates.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:29.980
Rigorovic.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.960
Boris Grigorovitch.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:32.520
Bond.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.460
James Bond, Jr.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:38.340
And this beautiful flower is Nadia Glasso.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.080
Her father is a Russian cosmonaut.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.700
Very nice to meet you.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.220
The pleasure is mine.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.340
Now, get to know each other and enjoy your stay at Moscow.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.060
My father has arranged a special trip for you.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:57.380
We have all been invited to the Soviet Space Center to watch the space station cosmonauts take off.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.970
James, can you hear...

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.630
Talking umbrella? You Westerners have such strange toys.

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:09.540
It's not a toy, Boris. It's, um, one of my classmates' inventions.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:16.480
Let me show you. You're coming in picture-perfect, IQ.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.060
Oh, just thought I'd tune in to see how you were doing.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:24.320
We were just heading to the Soviet Space Center to watch a rocket launch.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:27.500
Well, let me know what happens over and out.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.140
IQ, I need a favor.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.600
What's the matter, Trevor?

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:33.950
It's the Russians.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.890
I'm sure they're up to something.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:39.110
I want to borrow your video camera and catch them in the act.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.380
Show sequences five minutes and counting.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.280
Goodbye, Nardir, my darling.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.180
I'll see you in six months.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:51.340
Good luck, Daddy.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:52.680
I'm glad you could come.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:53.780
Enjoy the launch.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.960
What are you staring at?

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.980
How long do I need to hold this dumb f...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.940
IQ. I feel like an idiot.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.390
We just keep it steady, Cordell.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.130
I want to track the launch

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.530
on my computer. Commander Olenov?

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:15.660
Hey, I don't understand, James.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.860
He's been a friend of my family for

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.960
years, but he acted

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:21.350
as if he didn't even know me.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.780
Why don't we look into it?

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.520
The initial sequence is three minutes.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.900
All personnel clear the launch area.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.160
Krasov, here are the control codes for the superlaser.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.960
Be sure to program them into their computer as soon as you get to the space station.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:46.740
In his haste, the commander just didn't recognize you.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:53.960
Be your commander. It's me, Maddie Krasov.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:58.660
Why, yes, of course. Come to see your father off, have you?

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:11.470
And now that the secret's out, you're going to have to die with it.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:19.490
You see two minutes?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:48.920
No, no, no, no.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:04.450
It is no use, James. We'll never get out of these chains in time.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:10.100
I may be able to cut through them with the acetylene torch in my watch. Terrific.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.520
Initial sequence in 20 seconds and counting.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:14.680
Oh, James.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:24.600
We've got one last chance. With IQ's super sensitivity glove, I may be able to crack the combination on this padlock.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:29.240
Initial sequence in 10 seconds and counting. Nine.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:39.790
8, 7, 6, 3, 2, 1, ignition!

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:52.830
Too close. Looks like we've got trouble.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.690
The chameleon and scum are up to their old tricks.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.300
Perhaps I can be of help.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.970
You can tell the space authorities to have the cosmonaut.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.580
Don't look out for anything unusual.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:03.210
Where are you, Jane?

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.240
Hey, what about yours truly?

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:10.090
Come with us, Gordo, and help us find the Chameleon.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:13.720
Great, I'm putting this stupid thing away right now.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.390
Oh, no, you're happening out there, too.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.330
Aw, give me a break.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.590
We were lucky to get these past customs.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.590
We'd better keep them safe.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.740
I feel it is time.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.060
I was right.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:35.220
They must be planning some kind of sabotage.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.220
I better find Mr. Milbanks and show him this tape.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.970
Cosmonauts have just entered...

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:06.880
the control into the laser guidance computer now i can override their computer and control the laser

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:23.780
from here it's moving by itself i can't control it systems are jammed we're falling back to earth

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:29.720
this is soviet ground control and not authorized

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.740
Transmission is jamming the space station's guidance systems.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.820
All emergency personnel report to the launch area.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:40.320
James, James, I think I nearly...

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:44.730
Talking IQ.

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:50.590
My satellite dish umbrella may be able to pick up the chameleon's transmission signals.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:56.690
By feeding the signals back into my computer here, I can help you home in on the source point.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.050
Let's give it a try.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.970
Aim the umbrella handle...

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.700
and pan it back and forth across the horizon.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:05.000
You got it, bro.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:05.880
Hold it.

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:07.650
That's the strongest signal.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.280
North West.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:10.020
Let's go.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:14.960
That's right, sir.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:18.060
James Bond and Nadia are trying to find a chameleon now.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:20.710
Our agents have informed us that the chameleon

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.350
is working with Dr. DeRange.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:25.010
They've gained control of the space station laser.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:27.640
With it, they could vaporize your friends.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.870
We've got to warn James.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:41.340
This is a restricted area. No one is permitted beyond this point without a pass.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:45.840
We have a pass. Don't we, Dr. Drake?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:50.050
Yes! Let me show you!

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:29.500
It's the chameleon.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.200
with derange. Looks like

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:35.470
we've got company. It's

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.740
Bond. Let's give him a

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:38.760
warm welcome.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:47.640
You are the dog.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:30.940
From this leg.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:08.400
diamonds so this is what they're after it is lucky for your friends that someone spotted an

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:16.030
audience jeep we'll be at the treasury bunker any minute uh yo it's starting to feel like a

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:22.070
microwave oven in here we don't have very long james i think i may know how to stop that thing

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:29.970
with an umbrella iq you still there your signal's fading james but i can't hear you

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:34.120
Crack the laser guidance code and get me control of the laser.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:38.340
It's possible, but I'd need a much bigger computer than mine.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.200
We have a large computer here.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:44.240
Wire the umbrella into their I.O. port, and I'll see what I can do.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:57.200
The little problem here, James, your computer speaks Russian, and I don't.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.960
Oh, just do your best, IQ, and do it.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:14.550
fast what's the meaning of this noseworthy spies what russian spies that's what those so-called

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:23.570
exchange students really are oh that's absurd i've got it all on tape sir see for yourself

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:29.770
we were lucky to get these past customs we'd better

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:35.040
them safe until it is time this doesn't prove a thing they could have anything in those cases

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:44.100
exactly anything at all like secret plans poison gas high explosives high explosives

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:48.960
hey i suppose i should check it out and risk our lives not likely

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:58.370
the laser is almost through get a move on iq

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.350
We don't have more time!

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:07.570
Look, reach!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.680
Looks like we've got more company!

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:15.000
Maybe we should offer them something hot to Nibbalan!

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:32.380
through the bunker before they send the army after us.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:01.700
Control of the laser!

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:04.620
I think the hole is big enough to get through, come on!

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:11.100
KaiQ, you saved our necks!

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:19.610
To save you now!

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.200
We can take care of ourselves, can't we, Gordo?

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:23.460
No sweat, man!

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:50.490
Sit back, relax, baby, until the chameleon sings.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:05.240
Looks like you trapped yourself, dude.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:06.190
Guess again!

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:07.250
Full!

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:12.960
I'm on the right side of the bow!

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:18.610
It's going to get away with the diamonds!

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.120
IQ, contact the space station

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:24.180
and tell them to fire one more short laser burst down here.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:26.710
Thermative.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.040
Previous coordinates, I understand.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:41.920
Going to be concerned about derange?

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.410
We've just sealed your fate.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:46.590
I hope you have a very warm coat.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.490
It is very cold in Siberia.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:50.270
No!

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:58.970
Right over here, sir.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.920
They're opening the cases.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:07.500
What's going on here?

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.270
Trouble knows where the big trouble.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.110
Can you see this, Willis?

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:22.160
Glee IQ.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:28.250
Looks like your friend Trevor is doing his best to improve relations between the East and West.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.970
And worsen them with...

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:30.720
Milbanks.

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:01.480
Yeah.
